# Reference walk for the PageFlip spread check (docs/pageflip.md section 4.2). One instance, no
# peer, so every press turns exactly one page -- which makes this the ground truth the pair is
# measured against: a spread reader shows pages 0,2,4 on the left and 1,3,5 on the right, so every
# one of the pair's six screenshots must equal one of these six.
#
# Comparing the two halves against each other cannot express that. It can only say "same" or
# "different", and "different" is equally true of a pair that is one page apart and a pair that has
# desynced by nine.
log pageflip-solo: start
expect_timeout 60000
expect Entering activity: Home
wait 800
tap confirm
expect Entering activity: EpubReader
# First open builds the section cache.
wait 9000
screenshot /screenshots/pf-solo-00.bmp
tap down
wait 2500
screenshot /screenshots/pf-solo-01.bmp
tap down
wait 2500
screenshot /screenshots/pf-solo-02.bmp
tap down
wait 2500
screenshot /screenshots/pf-solo-03.bmp
tap down
wait 2500
screenshot /screenshots/pf-solo-04.bmp
tap down
wait 2500
screenshot /screenshots/pf-solo-05.bmp
log pageflip-solo: done
quit
